WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for t3-01-high-stakes-presence.mp3 — machine-transcribed on-device from the existing audio (SR-472). Not proofread.
NOTE Cues with ids phase-recognise/-regulate/-release/-rise mark where each step begins; js/saferise-poster.js reads them.

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:03.630
Something is about to happen.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:06.430
And you're the one they're all going to look at

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.970
You're probably not somewhere quiet.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.780
A car park, a stairwell, a cubicle.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:22.100
The corridor outside, that's where this was built to work, and you're not
going to get a quiet room. This works on the state you'd be walking in with.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:30.080
It leaves the thing itself entirely alone.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:38.590
What you say, how it lands, what happens after? The body goes first. The part
of you that knows how to handle this comes second.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.730
It's slower, but it's there.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.740
Most of the trouble lives in the gap between the two.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.660
The next few minutes close some of it. You don't need to keep track.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.270
I'll take you through

phase-recognise
00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:56.190
First, we recognise where this charge lives before any words arrive. Chest,
usually.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.080
Something tight and high.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:10.140
The throat, a lightness through the arms, hands that won't settle.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.880
Sometimes the stomach dropping.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:30.200
Now describe it in one word, agitated. Notice what that word doesn't say. It
doesn't say you're not ready.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.620
It doesn't say it's going to go badly

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:44.170
This is what a body does before something that matters. It would be stranger
if it didn't.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.230
The state is not a prediction.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.620
It's just a state

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.710
Now go one step deeper

00:01:52.220 --> 00:02:00.380
Underneath it, something is riding on this that goes past the room.

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:04.500
The fear of exposure of failing when eyes are on you.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.180
Or losing your footing when it counts most.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:17.070
Leave that fear where it is, nothing to solve here. Second, we regulate your
breathing and anchor your posture. Breathe in for four.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:18.680
And out for six.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.700
Longer out than in.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:21.970
Every time.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:31.680
Nobody can see you doing this. It works with your eyes open.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:32.810
In a lift.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:33.940
At a table.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.660
Bring your attention to the middle of your chest.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.350
Press your feet into the floor.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.480
Feel it push back.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.510
This state closes both.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:20.320
And a closed throat changes your voice before you've said anything. Let the
teeth come apart.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:27.650
Let the tongue drop.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:35.400
Thoughts will come, maybe a lot of them. That's what a mind does. And it
doesn't mean this isn't working.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.970
When one arrives, let it arrive.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:39.700
Don't push it away

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.040
Don't follow it

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:42.450
Don't finish it.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:52.480
A thought turning up isn't a thought asking you to act.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.260
If you notice yourself working hard at this

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:56.470
He's off.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.370
Watching takes no effort.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:07.310
- Effort means you've started fighting.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.590
Whether passes through a room

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:25.990
The room doesn't become the weather. Hold this quiet grounding before we take
the next step.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:39.610
Third, we release the mental loop of running the future. There are two
separate things going on right now.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.040
There's the state

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:44.110
Which turned up because this matters to you.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.950
And there's the pre-playing.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.230
Running the room in advance.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:55.450
The question you can't answer, the face in the third row.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.540
The moment it goes wrong,

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:01.820
Notice which version you keep running.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:12.760
It's the bad one. It's always the bad one. That isn't preparation.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:14.600
And it isn't caution either.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:18.050
Every pass through it puts your body back at the start

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:27.230
And it's using the attention you're going to need in the room.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.420
Let the state stand.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.140
And it's appropriate.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:44.010
Put down the pre-playing, offer a quiet word of thanks to your attention.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:06:00.817
And your heart, forgiving you clear awareness of what has been powering this
internal engine, the instinctual concern that your worth standing and truth

00:06:00.817 --> 00:06:02.420
needed frantic defense.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.180
Was entirely valid.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:10.770
Yet keeping that emergency system active in the background has been siphoning
off the energy you need for the room.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:15.420
Thank your body's protection mechanism for amping up to guard you.

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:18.930
And reassure it that you can steer from here.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:26.480
In the question,

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:32.380
Not what's wrong with me that I still get like this. Plenty of people who are
very good at this still get like this.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:36.680
What was this for? A body sharpens before something that counts.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:38.880
That's the whole point of the state.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.620
It's aimed at

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.340
And it's over shooting.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.580
You don't need the answer now.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Keep the question.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:49.160
It's worth coming back to when you're steadier.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.500
Now put the underlying fear where your breath is.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.010
And leave it there.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.820
If it was running out of time or losing control,

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:04.590
Let go of the bracing.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:07.630
None of it gets settled from inside this state.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:14.850
That's why it wa

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.240
Until you're out of

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:26.970
We rise into quiet, deliberate composure.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:35.120
Picture yourself from across the room.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:36.600
Waiting to go in.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:37.950
You're ked up

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:39.300
And you're ready.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:46.310
Both are true.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:50.000
Now picture the version of you that you'd want to be walking in.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:51.440
Same nerves.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:52.720
Same stakes.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:01.690
But you're the one deciding where your attention goes.

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:03.740
Not on how it all turns out.

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:05.640
On the first thirty seconds.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:07.230
Where do you stand?

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:08.810
What do your hands do?

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:10.380
What's your first sentence

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:12.190
Now step into it.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:14.000
The nerves are still there.

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:16.060
Your attention is where you put it.

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:18.440
Pick one thing you'll do this way.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:19.710
When you walk in.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:24.130
Once that moment has happened, look back at it and write down what was
different.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:31.850
One more slow breath.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:33.550
In for four.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:36.840
Notice how you are now.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:38.280
Different or not,

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:45.210
Either is fine.

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:46.920
Move your hands and feet.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:48.910
Feel the floor under you.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:00.760
Return to this guided meditation as often as you need to.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:02.550
Until you no longer do.
